Adapt RDO's rpm-master python-cliff.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(cliff 4.13.3, the 2026.1 upper-constraints pin).

    error: File not found: .../site-packages/cliff/tests

cliff 4.13.3 still ships cliff/tests in the sdist, but its pyproject build no
longer installs them into the wheel, so nothing lands in site-packages. The spec
both excludes that directory from the main package and packages it as
python3-cliff-tests; neither can work now.

Both lines are dropped. python3-cliff-tests is left declared but empty rather
than removed outright, because deleting a subpackage changes what an upgrade
sees, and nothing here consumes it either way.

diff -ur a/cliff/python-cliff.spec b/cliff/python-cliff.spec
--- a/python-cliff.spec	2026-09-28 17:43:40.131028444 +0000
+++ b/python-cliff.spec	2026-09-28 17:58:40.749567602 +0000
@@ -100,9 +100,7 @@
 %doc doc/ README.rst ChangeLog AUTHORS CONTRIBUTING.rst
 %{python3_sitelib}/%{modname}
 %{python3_sitelib}/%{modname}-*.dist-info
-%exclude %{python3_sitelib}/%{modname}/tests
 
 %files -n python3-%{modname}-tests
-%{python3_sitelib}/%{modname}/tests
 
 %changelog
